<title>USA: Venturian unit contract affirmed.</title>
<headline>Venturian unit contract affirmed.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venturian Corp said Thursday its Napco International Inc defense products unit has been informed that a protest against one of its U.S. Army contracts has been denied.</p>
<p>The protest had been filed by a competitor regarding an $11.6 million contract awarded to Napco for 401 kits for the upgrade of the M113 armored personnel carrier. The protest was denied by the U.S. General Accounting Office.</p>
<p>As a result of the protest, Venturian said that shipments, which were originally scheduled to begin in the third quarter of 1997 and completed in the first half of 1998, are now expected to commence in the fourth quarter of this year, but should be completed by mid-1998.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
